  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \n\nA lingering instability gradient is apparent in mixed layer CAPE\ngraphics late this evening from southwest through south-central \nOhio. This gradient was caused by the thunderstorm complex earlier \nthat moved through central Ohio into southeast Ohio. Moving across\nthis gradient is a developing westerly low-level jet. Radar trends\nshow clusters of showers and storms developing in this area. With\nunseasonable deep moisture in place, many of the 00Z CAMs show a\nstripe of heavy rain ranging from one to three inches. Have opted to\nissue a short-fuse flood watch due to flash flooding potential\novernight. Much of the guidance has these storms moving off to the\neast by sunrise.",
